    "notes": "Deliberate divergence beyond a fix: a scrimless drawer opens with show() and a z-index (base 1000, later drawers above) instead of upstream's manual popover (showPopover), because ui-common's Modal and notification stack are z-index surfaces a top-layer drawer would cover; aria-modal passes through; a scrimmed (modal) drawer provides its dialog through ModalPortalContext so ui-common's Modal opened inside renders there, in the top layer. Escape routing is upstream's. On an Astryx bump, keep these until ui-common's Modal and notification stack are top layer and Astryx passes aria-modal through. Since 0.7.7, core's private useModalOutlet (toast viewport hosted in an open modal drawer) and ModalAnnounceProvider (announcements from inside the modal drawer) are left out, as is LayerContentBoundary; the stateless helpers 0.7.7 added are inlined.",
